   "area_id": "co_ellingwood_point",
   "name": "Wrong Peak",
   "grade": "5.9",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "Climbed by mistake as Blanca's Northeast Face, though it is on Ellingwood Point. Described as chossy, with stout 5.9 and hairy gear placements. Start left of center on the face beneath a black roof that arcs rightward and opens to vertical climbing. Head directly up to a slight ledge where protection is moderate; pitch 2 is the same. Pitch 3 climbs to the angled gash rising south, and pitch 4 goes up the gash, heading south, to a belay stance. Pitch 5 goes straight up; near the end a roof (crux) must be mantled. Belay below if protection allows, or mount it and run the rope to a grassy ledge on the left; otherwise protection is suspect. Pitch 6 continues up to the slot on the left.",
